  <data key="d2">The the company distributes the remaining profits to shareholders according to their sharehold before extracting optional surplus from the remaining profits.&lt;SEP&gt;The the company must use surplus to compensate for losses or expand production and operations or not for compensating for losses.&lt;SEP&gt;The the company must complete profit distribution once one month after the shareholders' meeting approve the distribution plan.&lt;SEP&gt;&lt;The the company must retain a sufficient ratio of surplus from capital increase to ensure the company's capital structure.&lt;SEP&gt;&lt;The company adheres to a continuous and stable profit distribution policy.</data>
